  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 136 AM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nAnother chilly morning this morning, but with slight improvement in \nreadings by a couple of degrees or so. Dry air and calm conditions \nwill allow areas of frost for parts of the mountains, plateau, and \nnortheast TN into southwest VA again.\n\nFor the week ahead, longwave troughing will remain well into Canada \nwith ridging poking north between a closed upper low off of the Mid-\nAtlantic and another closed low off of the west coast. The western \nlow eventually phases with the mean flow, meanwhile the Atlantic one \nthat will bring coastal issues to parts of the Eastern Seaboard due \nto hardly any movement, will become enveloped and shunted east \ntowards the end of the week. No impacts here except persistent upper \nlevel ridging and surface high pressure.\n\nHighs breaking 70 return for much of the valley later this \nafternoon. Highs will then remain in the low to mid 70s range the \nrest of the forecast period into next weekend. A general \nwash/rinse/repeat each day with light winds, mostly sunny/clear \nskies, low humidity, and no precipitation for at least the \nforeseeable future.",
